# VoxState — environment variables (example)
# Copy to .env and fill in real values. Do not commit .env.

# --- Server ---
PORT=8080
ENV=development

# --- PostgreSQL ---
DATABASE_URL=postgres://voxstate:voxstate@localhost:5432/voxstate?sslmode=disable

# --- LiveKit (voice transport) --- wired in M6: the Go backend joins
# LiveKit rooms directly as a raw participant (LiveKit's Agents framework
# has no Go support — see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md). Tokens are minted
# server-side; never expose LIVEKIT_API_SECRET to a client.
LIVEKIT_URL=
LIVEKIT_API_KEY=
LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=

# --- Rime (TTS) --- wired in M6: hand-rolled REST client (no official
# Rime SDK exists in Go). RIME_MODEL_ID/RIME_SPEAKER/RIME_SAMPLE_RATE_HZ
# have sensible local defaults (coda/astra/24000) if left unset — see
# internal/config/config.go. samplingRate is always sent explicitly on
# every request; Rime's own docs are inconsistent about what an implicit
# default would be.
RIME_API_KEY=
RIME_MODEL_ID=coda
RIME_SPEAKER=astra
RIME_SAMPLE_RATE_HZ=24000

# --- Deepgram (STT) --- wired in M6: official Go SDK
# (deepgram-go-sdk/v3), prerecorded REST endpoint called once per
# segmenter.go-detected utterance.
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=

# --- LLM provider (reasoning/tool-calling) --- NOT wired. M5's Agent uses
# a deterministic KeywordPlanner (no network call, no API key) and M6's
# voice layer feeds it the same plain instruction text a real LLM
# provider would eventually replace this Planner with. These two vars
# are reserved for whichever future milestone actually adds one.
LLM_API_KEY=
LLM_MODEL=

# --- Frontend --- (wired in M8)
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8080
